  "name": "THROMBIN TIME",
  "code": "1585",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>1.Thrombin Time should be interpreted in conjunction with other coagulation assays like PT &amp; APTT to enhance diagnostic value.<br>2.Results should be clinically correlated.<br>3.Test conducted on Citrated plasma.</p>\n<p><br>Comments :<br>Thrombin Time (TT) measures the ability of exogenous thrombin to proteolyse fibrinogen. Thus it is used to characterize fibrinogen function. It is prolonged in conditions like hypofibrinogenemia, dysfibrinogenemia, presence of fibrin degradation products, antibody inhibitors of thrombin and in conditions with high concentrations of monoclonal immunoglobulins which interfere with fibrin monomer polymerization like Myeloma &amp; Macroglobulinemia.</p>",
